.TH SSHPUB 1 "September 2026" "sshpub 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sshpub \- download and manage SSH Pub public keys in authorized_keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sshpub add
.I user
.br
.B sshpub add
.I user/device[,device...]
.br
.B sshpub remove
.I user
.br
.B sshpub remove
.I user/device[,device...]
.br
.B sshpub list
.br
.B sshpub version
.br
.B sshpub upgrade
.SH DESCRIPTION
SSH Pub is a lightweight SSH public key management and distribution tool.
The CLI downloads public keys from SSH Pub, validates them, deduplicates them,
and safely writes them to the current user's authorized_keys file.
.PP
SSH Pub never reads or stores private keys.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add user
Download all enabled public keys for the user and add any missing keys.
.TP
.B add user/device[,device...]
Download one or more device keys. The server must not return keys for devices
that were not requested.
.TP
.B remove user
Remove all local SSH Pub-managed keys for the user.
.TP
.B remove user/device[,device...]
Remove local SSH Pub-managed keys for the selected devices.
.TP
.B list
List all valid public keys in authorized_keys and label them as SSHPUB or LOCAL.
.TP
.B version
Print the sshpub version.
.TP
.B upgrade
Ask SSH Pub whether a newer version is available. This command only runs when
the user invokes it, and it prints upgrade instructions without replacing the
binary.
.SH SECURITY
The CLI validates downloaded keys with golang.org/x/crypto/ssh, rejects
authorized_keys options, accepts only allowlisted ordinary SSH public key
algorithms, rejects OpenSSH certificates, verifies SSH Pub comments, and writes
authorized_keys atomically only after all validation succeeds.
.PP
The CLI does not provide SSH login, run a daemon or agent, collect telemetry,
automatically check for updates, automatically update itself, or modify sshd
configuration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
The authorized_keys file read and modified by sshpub.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure.
